WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.480
A ticket closes. Engineering says the fix is live.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.260
But the customer still can't get their work done.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.980
Rectify connects the complaint, the engineering evidence, and the customer's

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.080
actual workflow, then follows through until recovery is observed.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.080
Let's walk through it.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.400
We're using labelled local fixtures for this recording.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.070
Maya at Northstar reports an empty CSV export.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.700
Opening her Gmail thread creates a case using the trusted

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.880
customer directory. Investigate starts a real model turn.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.460
It reads the complaint, compares plausible GitHub issues, checks the

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.740
Slack rollout claim, and runs Northstar's export.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.480
The issue is closed, but the workflow check fails.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.630
Here's the gap: the request succeeded, but the expected records

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:56.100
are missing. Rectify records the evidence, creates a customer-impact issue

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.930
and a Slack handoff, and keeps the resolution message blocked.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.000
In ReportDesk, an operator enables the corrected export path.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.340
This is an explicit human configuration change, with an audit

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.710
event and a new revision.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.830
Recheck runs the same customer workflow again.

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:15.600
This time, it passes.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.040
Now the customer message is ready for review.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.260
Approval binds the recipient, wording, and passing check.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.350
For this fixture recording, the local helper submits a signed

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.000
approval through the same validation endpoint.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.560
The worker confirms one send.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.970
Sending isn't recovery. Maya opens ReportDesk in a customer session

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.520
and runs the export herself.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.660
The expected rows appear.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:46.039
Only that successful customer operation produces the signed outcome event.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:49.210
The customer has recovered, and cross-app updates are confirmed.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:55.040
Rectify keeps engineering status, verification, notification, and recovery separate.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:57.080
Every conclusion has evidence.
